Optional language identification
The `language-id` feature builds in the lingua crate and its language models
(Apache-2.0). lingua's authors trained those models on the Leipzig Corpora
Collection (Wortschatz, Leipzig University), whose texts are licensed under
CC BY-NC 4.0; the models contain n-gram statistics, not the texts.

Earlier revisions
Revisions before fb41dd1 also contained two third-party tokenizer files in
testdata/tokenizers, since moved to docudis-ner:
- sentencepiece.json: XLM-RoBERTa's SentencePiece vocabulary, MIT License,
  Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc. and its affiliates.
- wordpiece.json: multilingual BERT's WordPiece vocabulary, Apache-2.0,
  Copyright 2018 The Google AI Language Team Authors.
